dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saadiqbal-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saadiqbal-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saadiqbal-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/activity.nearbuilders.org/commits/49764ccf4f82fdadacd979b288547298c6f9ffe5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:43:31Z","email":"saadiqbal.dev@outlook.com","name":"saadiqbal-dev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:43:31Z","email":"saadiqbal.dev@outlook.com","name":"saadiqbal-dev"},"message":"docs: add an administrator guide and expand source onboarding\n\nActivity had no documentation for Platform Administrators, who review\nsources, set trust and score multipliers, and hide events. The admin\nreview and trust controls are only visible on /activity-sources when the\nsigned-in user has the admin role, and hiding an event has no UI at all,\nso the operations were effectively undiscoverable.\n\ndocs/admin-guide.md covers the role model, promoting administrators\n(database bootstrap for the first, the auth admin API afterwards),\nreviewing sources, trust and multipliers, hiding events, health checks,\nand what administrators cannot do.\n\nTwo behaviours worth knowing are documented because they surprise people:\nediting a source returns it to the review queue and unbinds its Signing\nIdentity if the NEAR account changed, and approval is one-way, since\nrevoking API keys is owner-only and no route disables an approved source.\n\nSection 1 of the integration guide becomes a real walkthrough of the\nbrowser flow, including that the binding transaction must come from the\nsource''s exact NEAR account, and a pointer to GitHub polling. The README\ngains a guide index.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014DEs6bFdQvtKDkSHHecRQU","tree":{"sh