rl":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype--guest/commits/4e0a145b4cd983610d01292418dba259b78d7a02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T00:31:46Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T16:24:37Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"message":"Deploy jerry to Netlify as a federated remote\n\nnetlify.toml carries the three things a module federation remote needs that an\nordinary static site does not. JERRY_ORIGIN is pinned so a Netlify built copy\nbakes the deployed origin into its chunk URLs rather than falling back to\nlocalhost, since world resolves them from a page on its own origin. Every asset\nsends Access-Control-Allow-Origin, because world loads remoteEntry.js cross\norigin as a module script, and Timing-Allow-Origin so world''s probe still reads\nreal transfer sizes. The catch all redirect serves the app shell for jerry''s\nstandalone wouter routes; static files match first, so remoteEntry.js and the\nhashed chunks are unaffected.\n\nLive at https://jerry-remote.netlify.app. The world side entry is\nhttps://jerry-remote.netlify.app/remoteEntry.js.","tree":{"sha":"09346676f2bfc662e92da474c9a397034f5fd051","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype--guest/git/trees/09346676f2bfc662e92da474c9a397034f5fd051"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype--guest/git/commits/4e0a145b4cd983610d01292418dba259b78d7a02","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":