globe): add failing test for 3D hexagonal binning financial volume layer\n\n* feat(globe): implement 3D hexagonal binning layer for global financial FX volume\n\n* docs(adr): add ADR 0064 for market sessions migration to /kurs\n\n* wip: test(market): add failing test for market sessions migration to /kurs\n\n* feat(apps): migrate global FX market sessions to /kurs and purify /time for world cities\n\n* docs(adr): add ADR 0065 for live USGS and BMKG earthquake API integration\n\n* wip: test(quake): add failing test for USGS and BMKG live earthquake service\n\n* feat(quake): integrate USGS and BMKG live earthquake feeds with SWR caching and offline fallback\n\n* docs(adr): add ADR 0066 for eliminating Plotly and fe-2\n\n* wip: test(globe): add failing tests for complete elimination of Plotly and fe-2\n\n* feat(globe): eliminate Plotly and fe-2, focusing purely on 3D globe visualization in fe-1 (ADR 0066)\n\n* docs(adr): add ADR 0067 for clean globe typography and glyph elimination\n\n* wip: test(globe): add failing test suite for clean typography and glyph elimination\n\n* feat(globe): purify 3D pin typography, eliminate ''??'' artifacts and arbitrary icons (ADR 0067)\n\n* docs(adr): add ADR 0068 for dedicated earthquake controls and bottom dock\n\n* wip: test(quake): add failing test suite for dedicated earthquake UI components\n\n* feat(quake): implement dedicated QuakeControls, QuakeBottomDock, and QuakeTooltip with live seismic ticker (ADR 0068)\n\n* fix(quake): wrap QuakeControls in absolute floating container so filter panel renders at top-right\n\n* docs(adr): add ADR 0069 for world cities radiant dots and population scaling\n\n* wip: test(capitals): add failing test suite for world cities radiant dots and population scaling\n\n* feat(capitals): implement world cities radiant dots with population scaling on /capitals and solar colors on /time (ADR 0069)\n\n* wip: test(population): add failing tests for population app and live service\n\n* docs(adr): add ADR 0070 for Indonesian timezone pillars LOD hierarchy\n\n* wip: test(time): add failing test suite for Indonesian cities LOD hierarchy\n\n* feat(time): harmonize indonesian timezone pillars LOD with zoom-aware test\n\n* feat(population): implement population world microapp with World Bank API and offline dataset\n\n* feat(time): harmonize indonesian timezone pillars LOD with zoom-aware test\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: rafliiar17 <rafztesting@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"66e5a99808240696189d17a8b46547ec0743345a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafliiar17/buanasphere/git/trees/66e5a99808240696189d17a8b46547ec0743345a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafliiar17/buanasphere/git/commits/b3c8fe650653b4b1deea1ee8cd7bf887ae1336d6","verification":{"payload":"tree 66e5a99808240696189d17a8b46547ec0743345a\nparent ae375e79e885ffa2f30e7bd2c9f74ab1fd6c94df\nauthor IamRFZ <39895896+rafliiar17@users.noreply.github.com> 1788464986 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788464986 +0700\n\nfeat: BuanaSphere 2.0 Mega-Upgrade — 3D Hexbin, Dedicated Quake UI, Live USGS/WorldBank APIs, Clean Typography, and Population World Microapp (#42)\n\n* docs(adr): add ADR 0060 for frontend-2 canonical globe.gl migration\n\n* feat(frontend-2): initialize canonical globe.gl frontend architecture and migrate core features\n\n* docs(adr): add ADR 0061 for fe1 modular globe.gl and dynamic filtering\n\n* feat(fe1): modularize globe.gl engine layers with full dynamic filtering support\n\n* docs(adr): add ADR 0062 for full replacement of FE1 globe with GlobeScene\n\n* feat(fe1): replace monolithic globe with declarative GlobeScene component architecture\n\n* feat(fe1): apply fe-2 photorealistic earth texture and luminous cyan palette to GlobeScene\n\n* docs(adr): add ADR 0063 for 3D hexagonal binning financial volume layer\n\n* wip: test(globe): add failing test for 3D hexagonal binning financial volume layer\n\n* feat(globe): implement 3D hexagonal binning layer for global financial FX volume\