i.github.com/users/sudoitir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudoitir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudoitir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudoitir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudoitir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudoitir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sudoitir/artemis-studio/commits/df682778584120dcb64db1d76e9aab704115a3f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:39:50Z","email":"sudoit.ir@gmail.com","name":"Mahdi Amirabdollahi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:39:50Z","email":"sudoit.ir@gmail.com","name":"Mahdi Amirabdollahi"},"message":"build: make the justfile and scripts portable to bash 3.2 and BSD tools\n\ndev-up and demo wait with `docker compose up --wait` instead of `timeout`, which macOS\nlacks. qa-seed.sh computes its expiry date in python3 instead of GNU `date -d`.\nscripts/lib/signin.sh no longer uses `path` or `status` as variable names, which zsh ties\nto PATH and its exit status, and finds its own directory when sourced from zsh.\nconfig-e2e.sh prints a byte count without BSD `wc` padding. CLAUDE.md records the rule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a97768cac078cd1ec05c3472b8affb79a78ed9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sudoitir/artemis-studio/git/trees/2a97768cac078cd1ec05c3472b8affb79a78ed9d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sudoitir/artemis-studio/git/commits/df682778584120dcb64db1d76e9aab704115a3f0","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a97768cac078cd1ec05c3472b8affb79a78ed9d\nparent 1a52ca20e37101565738a3f10e150f7f8bbc8ff8\nauthor Mahdi Amirabdollahi <sudoit.ir@gmail.com> 1791463190 +0200\ncommitter Mahdi Amirabdollahi <sudoit.ir@gmail.com> 1791463190 +0200\n\nbuild: make the justfile and scripts portable to bash 3.2 and BSD tools\n\ndev-up and demo 