follows on a request page, not its state twice\n\nEvery outcome notice on a request''s page repeated the state the header\nbadge already showed (\"Refused when run\" twice, for example); each now\nsays what follows from it: \"Nothing was changed\", \"It will not run\",\n\"Done\". A closed request''s changes are headed \"What it did\" or\n\"What it asked for\" rather than \"What will happen\", the page no longer\ncalls every request \"held\" after it ended, and a requester''s own\nwaiting request no longer shows an empty Decision section that repeated\nwho decides.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4c2ec06dd2c4d09210a6cb797d99d95aa5b26d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sudoitir/artemis-studio/git/trees/e4c2ec06dd2c4d09210a6cb797d99d95aa5b26d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sudoitir/artemis-studio/git/commits/5a67c55de0ece3f07c1891a697f1d3bd60884e94","verification":{"payload":"tree e4c2ec06dd2c4d09210a6cb797d99d95aa5b26d0\nparent ea8c89cbdcaa0108cd846bed0bd2fb6bb1412084\nauthor Mahdi Amirabdollahi <sudoit.ir@gmail.com> 1791432682 +0200\ncommitter Mahdi Amirabdollahi <sudoit.ir@gmail.com> 1791432682 +0200\n\nfix(approvals): say what follows on a request page, not its state twice\n\nEvery outcome notice on a request''s page repeated the state the header\nbadge already showed (\"Refused when run\" twice, for example); each now\nsays what follows from it: \"Nothing was changed\", \"It will not run\",\n\"Done\". A closed request''s changes are headed \"What it did\" or\n\"What it asked for\" rather than \"What will happen\", the page no longer\ncalls every request \"held\" after it ended, and a requester''s own\nwaiting request no longer shows an empty Decision section that repeated\nwho decides.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEgW2y6iVBnyvPOVkLsHEkFZDkDC4FAmrHF+oACgkQsHEkFZDk\nDC5dKQ/+OoMPkQE6ayM/y3qVwaKnp4OOsciG