tps://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/commits/46a1d953ecb316d38932024eb8503a2b8bbd4c73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T07:58:14Z","email":"peter.gabor04@gmail.com","name":"Péter Gábor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T07:58:14Z","email":"peter.gabor04@gmail.com","name":"Péter Gábor"},"message":"Harden projection USB checkpoint runtime\n\nRefactors the Linux USB/IPC checkpoint flow to be safer and more deterministic during the version-only phase. The daemon now uses safer Unix-socket binding/shutdown behavior, limits and times out IPC clients, and rejects non-checkpoint IPC commands. USB runtime handling was tightened around AOAP handover ownership, candidate filtering, cancellation, setup timeouts, and stale-result handling so unplug/re-enumeration behaves predictably without advancing to TLS/media. Version framing and response parsing now enforce stricter plaintext/length/validity checks and distinguish disconnect/read-error paths. Added broad native tests for socket lifecycle, framing edge cases, AOAP failures, replug races, and checkpoint cancellation behavior, plus docs updates (runbook/checkpoint expectations) and a Rust toolchain bump to 1.88.","tree":{"sha":"bfd7110d4a169dafc060013dc9a6a7806f40e664","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/git/trees/bfd7110d4a169dafc060013dc9a6a7806f40e664"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/git/commits/46a1d953ecb316d38932024eb8503a2b8bbd4c73","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30007117?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Gaborboy95","id":30007117,"login":"Gaborboy95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMDA3MTE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Gaborboy95/project-argo/commit/46a1d953ecb316d38932024eb8503a2b8bbd4c73","node_id":"C_kwDOUM2-m9oAKDQ2YTFkOTUzZWNiMzE2ZDM4OTMyMDI0ZWI4NTAzYTJiOGJiZDRjNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Gaborboy95/project-argo/commit/cca6252ccc6ebb8b44ddb8c5ee438c7b6f170aae","sha":"cca6252ccc6ebb8b44ddb8c5ee438c7b6f170aae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/commits/cca6252ccc6ebb8b44ddb8c5ee438c7b6f170aae"}],"sha":"46a1d953ecb316d38932024eb8503a2b8bbd4c73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/commits/46a1d953ecb316d38932024eb8503a2b8bbd4c73"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30007117?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Gaborboy95","id":30007117,"login":"Gaborboy95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMDA3MTE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/commits/cca6252ccc6ebb8b44ddb8c5ee438c7b6f170aae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:52:28Z","email":"peter.gabor04@gmail.com","name":"Péter Gábor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:52:28Z","email":"peter.gabor04@gmail.com","name":"Péter Gábor"},"message":"Add USB runtime and IPC snapshot server\n\nRefactors `argo-projectiond` into an async Tokio daemon with separate IPC and USB runtime modules, including watch-based runtime state broadcasting and graceful shutdown handling. Adds a projection runtime snapshot model plus payload writer helpers, and introduces a Linux USB state machine that handles AOAP probing, re-enumeration, endpoint selection, and Android Auto version negotiation up to `VersionResponse` (explicitly stopping before TLS). Tests and docs were expanded to cover frame decoding/encoding boundaries, transport negotiation behavior, USB lifecycle edge cases, and Milestone 14.1 validation steps.","tree":{"sha":"ab007eabf218021f59e5bbb74f5ee477d09cdcf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/git/trees/ab007eabf218021f59e5bbb74f5ee477d09cdcf7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/git/commits/cca6252ccc6ebb8b44ddb8c5ee438c7b6f170aae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_u