lse,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/commits/38a3685a0a3648525dfd938f42a226d9d111792b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T17:39:14Z","email":"peter.gabor04@gmail.com","name":"Péter Gábor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T17:39:14Z","email":"peter.gabor04@gmail.com","name":"Péter Gábor"},"message":"Add audio service, PipeWire backend, and controls\n\nIntroduces a backend-neutral audio domain (`AudioService`, snapshots, types, and in-memory backend) with persisted settings for volume, mute, balance/fader, EQ, output preference, and source focus/ducking policy. Wires audio composition into bootstrap, updates Settings to render real audio controls, and adds backend selection with opt-in PipeWire `wpctl` integration (safe default remains disabled).\n\nAdds a Veloce vehicle audio control bridge for fixed command topics, extracts shared plugin authorization logic, extends vehicle signals for normalized audio button inputs, and adds an example `audio_policy` plugin plus simulation scenario. Includes comprehensive tests for audio service behavior, backend selection, dependency boundaries, vehicle bridge authorization, and integration coverage, along with developer docs for Linux/IVI audio checks.","tree":{"sha":"77a3b4940cc1e0dc8549aaac9364ce95e2f8ba77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/git/trees/77a3b4940cc1e0dc8549aaac9364ce95e2f8ba77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/git/commits/38a3685a0a3648525dfd938f42a226d9d111792b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30007117?v=4","events_ur