"organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/commits/f7524daa7c8043351ef10b12ed40239ee195ccd9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:47:53Z","email":"peter.gabor04@gmail.com","name":"Péter Gábor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:47:53Z","email":"peter.gabor04@gmail.com","name":"Péter Gábor"},"message":"Add transport lifecycle and shutdown support\n\nIntroduce a VehicleTransportLifecycle abstraction (with NoOp implementation) and wire it through Veloce CAN selection and app bootstrap. Add RestartableCanProvider to allow recreating the physical CAN delegate and preserve logical subscriptions across transport quiesce/resume. Extend HostPowerController with powerOff and update LinuxSystemdHostPowerController to run systemctl poweroff. Refactor HostPowerRequestBridge to accept a transport lifecycle, handle both suspend and shutdown requests, quiesce/resume the CAN transport, serialize concurrent host-power operations, and improve diagnostics. Add comprehensive tests, example battery_protection plugin, updated can_decoder manifest, and a fake-systemctl tool and README for safe local testing.","tree":{"sha":"21b2d4e209c508f085bbcbfe902d332124b89a39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/git/trees/21b2d4e209c508f085bbcbfe902d332124b89a39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/git/commits/f7524daa7c8043351ef10b12ed40239ee195ccd9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30007117?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Gaborboy95","id":30007117,"login":"Gaborboy95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMDA3MTE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Gaborboy95/project-argo/commit/f7524daa7c8043351ef10b12ed40239ee195ccd9","node_id":"C_kwDOUM2-m9oAKGY3NTI0ZGFhN2M4MDQzMzUxZWYxMGIxMmVkNDAyMzllZTE5NWNjZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Gaborboy95/project-argo/commit/61e0271c9eda6957f0949e04471f298419c5631f","sha":"61e0271c9eda6957f0949e04471f298419c5631f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/commits/61e0271c9eda6957f0949e04471f298419c5631f"}],"sha":"f7524daa7c8043351ef10b12ed40239ee195ccd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/commits/f7524daa7c8043351ef10b12ed40239ee195ccd9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30007117?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Gaborboy95","id":30007117,"login":"Gaborboy95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMDA3MTE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaborboy95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/commits/61e0271c9eda6957f0949e04471f298419c5631f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T09:46:20Z","email":"peter.gabor04@gmail.com","name":"Péter Gábor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T09:46:20Z","email":"peter.gabor04@gmail.com","name":"Péter Gábor"},"message":"Add host suspend bridge and power policy plugin\n\nIntroduce host power control plumbing with a configurable backend (`ARGO_HOST_POWER_BACKEND`), including a disabled default and a Linux systemd implementation that runs `systemctl suspend`. Wire a new `HostPowerRequestBridge` into bootstrap to accept suspend requests only from authorized active-integration plugins, gate them by standby state/episode, flush settings before suspend, and handle lifecycle cleanup and diagnostics.\n\nAdd an example Lua `power_policy` plugin that publishes one suspend request per sleep episode after a delay, update integration docs, and expand tests across controller selection, Linux command behavior, bridge authorization/concurrency/lifecycle behavior, and the example vehicle integration flow.","tree":{"sha":"15c83d39325f97436797fc700e2c69882137dc10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/git/trees/15c83d39325f97436797fc700e2c69882137dc10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gaborboy95/project-argo/git/commits/61e0271c9eda6957f0949e04471f2